  "body": "Follow-up of #1953 (item 2: behaviour tests do not depend on the look).\n\nThe browser tree rows are painted, not widgets. They have no AccessKit node. So behaviour tests find a row by arithmetic: `BROWSER_TREE_TOP = 150.0`, `BROWSER_EYE_X = 220.0`, `row * theme::current().row_height`, and context menu rows at `DROP_GAP + k * row_height`. A refit that changes the row height, the header or the eye column breaks them.\n\nTests (inventory comment on #1953):\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests.rs`: `stock_eye_hides_the_viewport_stock…`, `dragging_an_operation_row_reorders…`, `operations_heading_menu_pastes…`, `operation_type_menu_requires_confirmation`, `operation_menu_suppresses_and_sets…`\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/program_entry.rs`: `the_operation_menu_adds_an_entry…`\n\nWhat to do:\n1. Give each painted browser row, its eye toggle and the rows of the tree context menu an AccessKit node with a label.\n2. Change the tests to find the row by label. A drag uses the node's rect.\n3. Remove `BROWSER_TREE_TOP` and `BROWSER_EYE_X`.\n\nDone means: no behaviour test computes a browser row position, and the `#[test]` count of `crates/ui` does not go down.\n",
